    "text": {
     "en": "Gundappa has some land with tall coconut trees. Count the trees from the top view.\nHe plucked 5 coconuts from each tree. If there are 6 trees, that is 6 groups of 5, or 30 coconuts.\nMuniamma makes plates and cups in a pattern. Trays of laddoos and peda are arranged the same way and stacked, so count one tray and multiply.\nPatterns with money: Shirley and Shiv arrange play money of 1, 2, 5 and 10 to show amounts like ₹36, ₹125 and ₹183.\nCounting in groups and finding the pattern is faster than counting one by one."
    }
